  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nQuiet weather is expected across the Middle Ohio Valley as a ridge \nbuilds east today and Tuesday. Drier conditions are also expected to \nprevail for Wednesday, though the ridge begins to recede as a front \napproaches from the northwest.\n\nDaytime temperatures start out a touch above normal and then trend \nwarmer by a few degrees each day, potentially buoying highs into the \nlow 90s for parts of the lowlands by mid week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nChances of showers and thunderstorms overspread the area as a cold \nfront approaches Wednesday night and then progresses southeast \nthrough the area on Thursday. \n\nPrecipitable water values in the neighborhood of 1.5 to 2 inches are \nlikely to support heavy downpours within storms. This, combined with \npotential for training storms, will prompt at least a marginal risk \nof excessive rainfall on Thursday. In addition to moisture, a \ndecent amount of shear is likely to be present in the vicinity \nof the front; however, model soundings continue to exhibit an \nunimpressive amount of instability which should curtail the risk\nof severe weather.\n\nWidespread activity tapers off behind the front Thursday night,\nthough lingering moisture and the arrival of a shortwave could \nprompt a few additional showers and storms at times late week \ninto the weekend.",
